dear Educators dear Learners their  citizens and Friends  we all have classmates colleagues or  family members with dyslexia  individuals who are intelligent and  talented  but who are often stigmatized and feel  shame  simply because they have a different way  of learning  according to the European dyslexia  Association  around 12 percent of the global  population has the condition  this means one in eight people in our  society  both have a disability and a gift  to see the world differently  for too long we have overlooked the  power of dyslexic thinking  and this must change  and this is why through Education and  Research the European Union is helping  to empower dyslexic individuals  in 2022 together with our member states  we adopted the so-called Pathways to  school Success  it includes best practices to make our  classrooms more inclusive  first of all through targeted And Timely  support  which requires early detection of  dyslexia  thanks to our Horizon Euro program  we're funding such projects like change  dyslexia which is making early diagnosis  possible and scalable  second we recommend equipping teachers  and parents with the skills and  resources they need to provide support  including through open online courses  thanks to our Erasmus Plus program  we have helped to develop the first  European course about learning disorders  and perhaps most importantly third  let us always be open to new ways of  learning and providing encouragement  to all Learners regardless of age  especially those with disabilities  and this is why I welcome any  international support or attention to  dyslexia  dyslexia is an obstacle we can overcome  together as a society  the European Union is at your side in  fact  just two weeks ago we registered a  European citizens initiative  on specific learning disabilities  including dyslexia  we will follow up with a European  response  to ensure that access to education  and success in life  is a right to all  thank you very much for your attention
 

